{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1a0d1e0-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
    "name": "BloodLink — Local Backend",
    "description": "Full local test collection for bloodlink-services (core-api + chat-api), matching docs/api-contract.md.\n\nSETUP:\n1. Import the companion 'BloodLink Local.postman_environment.json' and select it (top-right environment picker).\n2. Start both servers: `cd core-api && npm run dev` (port 4000) and `cd chat-api && npm run dev` (port 4001).\n3. Run '00 Health' first to confirm both are up.\n4. Run 'Auth' folder top to bottom for a normal donor account — check-email creates + sends the OTP, read it from your Gmail inbox (or the core-api terminal log if RESEND/GMAIL isn't configured), paste it into verify-otp/set-password. The 'token' collection variable auto-saves after set-password/login.\n5. For the Organizer/Staff-only folders, see each folder's description for how to flip isOrganizer/isHospitalStaff (a manual DB update, per decision #3 — there's no self-serve endpoint).\n6. Most `:id` path segments (driveId, slotId, requestId, donationId...) are collection variables auto-captured by 'Tests' scripts on the requests that create them — run creates before reads/updates in each folder.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
